**How to implement.** The reference pipeline's transcribed expectations get ONE home in test support, which `MuellerReconstructionTests` and AT-1 (S12.1) share (001 §Q AT-1 'the transcribed expected literals move from the §7.2 test body into one shared reference module, which both tests open. The test reads no file for its expectations (spec 0044 §8.5)'; 001 §S10 third bullet 'move its expected literals into one shared reference module'; the S10.3 brief 'dataMatrixTol moves with them'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step every expected literal of the Stage-1 and section 7.2 facts exists once, in `MuellerReference`. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs`: `module MuellerReference` in `namespace BerremanTestSupport`, the shape of `BiaxialSample.fs` (step 345), compiled after `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` through one `<Compile Include="MuellerReference.fs" />` line in `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, with no comment and no reference added (Domain since step 344, Optimization since step 345). The module opens only what its values need. Its doc, one to three lines: the optics-mueller reference pipeline's full-precision results, transcribed from `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/reference_step1_summary.json` and `reference_step2_linear_summary.json` (step 329), which `MuellerReconstructionTests` and AT-1 assert against, so no test reads a file for its expectations (spec 0044 §8.5; spec 0050 S10.3). Each value is born elevated (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin … This holds for test fixtures too'), and each value's doc, one line, names its summary key. In this order: (a) The two bands, moved from the class bindings `stage1Tol` and `dataMatrixTol` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:stage1Tol`, `:dataMatrixTol`) with their values `1.0e-12` and `1.0e-9` and their docs, and the comment block above `stage1Tol` (the spec 0044 §8.5 / §9 bands and their observed figures) with its text as step 329 leaves it. (b) The Stage-1 constants of `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values`, from `reference_step1_summary.json`: `darkMean` = `DarkMean 869.666` (`dark_mean_avg_total`); `lpAnalyzerZero` = `Angle.degree 155.44011830109392<deg>` (`lp_lp_anchor.zero_angle_deg`); `cplAnalyzerZero` = `Angle.degree 96.99613336321012<deg>` (`cpl_analyzer_from_lp_cpl.zero_angle_deg`); `cplAnalyzerRetardance` = `Retardance.degree 83.66804489441891<deg>` (`cpl_analyzer_from_lp_cpl.retardance_raw_deg`, the magnitude stage 1 derives); `cplSourceAxisOffset` = `Angle.degree 39.31100224361002<deg>` and `cplSourceRetardance` = `Retardance.degree 82.55344158462403<deg>` (`cpl_source_from_cpl_lp.source_theta_relaxed_model.theta_rel_deg` and `.retardance_deg`). Each of these degree literals comes back bit for bit from `.degrees` (checked when this spec was authored), so every comparison stays exact. (c) The section 7.2 values, from `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`: `qzMatrix`, `lrMatrix` and `combinedMatrix`, the `MuellerMatrix`es of `qz_matrix`, `lr_matrix` and `combined_matrix`, built from the literals the fact's `expectedQz`, `expectedLr` and `expectedComb` hold today (`RealMatrix4x4.create … |> MuellerMatrix`); `cascadeFrobenius`, `cascadeMeanAbs` and `cascadeMaxAbs`, the `MatrixDeviation`s 0.5714178795538456, 0.11328628636347338 and 0.26806464658062423 (`combined_vs_product_matrix.frobenius_norm`, `.mean_abs_entry_diff`, `.max_abs_entry_diff`); and `cascadeLargestDeltaPositions : Set<MuellerRowIndex * MuellerColumnIndex>`, the 0-indexed positions (3, 3) and (3, 1) of the two largest `delta_matrix` magnitudes, with the fact's spec 0044 note on them cut to one to three lines. (d) `excludedPoints : ExcludedPoint list`, the one point of the reference's `EXCLUDED_POINTS` (`Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_glue.py:22`, in `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` from step 329): experiment `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`, description 140°, capture index 17. It is the caller's data to the reconstruction (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:ExcludedPoint`, spec 0042 §0). (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` reads each of them as `MuellerReference.<name>` (`BerremanTestSupport` is open since step 344). It deletes `stage1Tol`, `dataMatrixTol` and the comment block above them. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` compares `darkMean` with `MuellerReference.darkMean.value` and each angle or retardance through `.degrees` of its `MuellerReference` value, in the same order and at `MuellerReference.stage1Tol`; its provenance comment says, in one to three lines, that the expected values are `MuellerReference`'s (spec 0050 S10.3). The section 7.2 fact deletes `expectedQz`, `expectedLr`, `expectedComb`, its local `excluded` and its three metric literals, and reads their `MuellerReference` values. It compares at `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` and checks its two largest-delta positions, now enumerated as `(MuellerRowIndex i, MuellerColumnIndex j)`, against `MuellerReference.cascadeLargestDeltaPositions`; its comments that name the summary say the values are `MuellerReference`'s. `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)` reads `MuellerReference.excludedPoints` in place of its local copy of the same point (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a re-transcribed constant is a defect). The class doc's spec 0044 §8.5 bullet adds that the expectations live in `BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference` (spec 0050 S10.3); no other comment changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every computed value and every expected value is the same double, so each assertion compares the same numbers. No test is added or removed. The test support project is outside the ELEV analyzers' scope (`.elevation-analyzers.json:13-21`, as step 344 records), so nothing under `Elevation/` changes.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` MUST declare `BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference` holding the two bands, the six Stage-1 constants, the three section 7.2 matrices, the three cascade metrics, the two largest-delta positions and the excluded point, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST hold none of these literals and read them from the module; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.
